  "notes": [
    {
      "marker": "1.",
      "text": "AIST/BMEG/CENG/CSCI/EEEN/ELEG/ENER/ENGG/ESTR/FTEC/IERG/MAEG/MATH/MIEG/SEEM/STAT required and major elective courses at 2000 and above level as well as MATH1025/1028, 1030/1038, and 1090/1098 will be included in the calculation of Major GPA for honours classification, excluding courses in Faculty Package and Foundation courses.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "2.",
      "text": "Students are advised to take some courses of the University Core Requirements or Major courses in summer sessions to reduce their course load in regular terms.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[a]",
      "text": "Students transferred to the programme can choose either set of the Major Programme Requirement.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[b]",
      "text": "Students who fail MATH1010/1018 in Term 1 will have to retake the course in Term 2.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[c]",
      "text": "Students who have declared to specialize in the ELITE Stream will be required to complete 6 units of ESTR4998 and 4999 to substitute for IERG4998 and 4999.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[d]",
      "text": "Details of the entrance and coursework requirements, and declaration procedures for the ELITE Stream can be found at the ELITE website (https://www.erg.cuhk.edu.hk/erg/elite). Non-ELITE Engineering students may be allowed to take ESTR courses. Students are required to seek approval from their respective Major Programmes for using ESTR courses taken to fulfill the Major Programme Requirement. Details are available at the ELITE website.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[e]",
      "text": "Students can use up to 9 units of courses which have been taken to fulfill the requirements of items 1 to 4 above to fulfill the elective requirements of the ELITE Stream. Item 3(c) Research Component Courses will not be included in these 9 units. A full list of ESTR courses is available at the ELITE website.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[f]",
      "text": "Students can use AIST/BMEG/CENG/CSCI/EEEN/ELEG/ENGG/IERG/MAEG/SEEM research postgraduate courses at 5000 level to substitute for ESTR courses at 3000 or 4000 level, subject to the approval of the Stream Director and the Associate Dean (Education).",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[g]",
      "text": "The requirement of at least 3 units of Engineering courses at 5000 level is a requirement for the ELITE Stream only. It should not be interpreted as a requirement of the Major Programme.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    }
  ],
  "supplementary": [
    "For students admitted via the Faculty of Science (under the Mathematics Enrichment Stream).",
    "1. Science Faculty Package:",
    "Group C: MATH1010/1018 Group E: STAT1011 A course from the following Group A: LSCI1001 or 1002 Group B: CHEM1070 or 1072 or 1280 Group D: PHYS1001 or 1002 or 1111 or 1113",
    "2. Foundation Courses:",
    "ENGG1110/ESTR1002, MATH1025/1028, MATH1030/1038",
    "3. Required Courses:",
    "(a) CSCI2100/ESTR2102, CSCI3160/ESTR3104, IERG2060/ESTR2304, IERG2080/ESTR2306, IERG2310/ESTR2300, IERG2820, IERG3080/ESTR3308, IERG3310/ESTR3310, IERG3800, 3820, MATH1090/1098, 2010/2018, 2020/2028, 2040/2048, 2050/2058, 2060/2068, 2070/2078, 2230, MIEG2051/ESTR2360, MIEG2440/ESTR2362",
    "(b) 3 units to be counted from ONE of the following courses: AIST1110, CSCI1120/ESTR1100, CSCI1130/ESTR1102, IERG1080",
